Subject: [PATCH 14/15] shader: wave64 reduce covers first lanes on the
 wave-path assumption

The five low-rate reductions still refused after the strict uniform_control
gate: their reduction blocks are behind lane branches, which uniform_control
rejects. A lane branch does not split the two host waves (both execute both
sides, masked); only a scalar branch can, and VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE already
assumes both halves compute the same scalars. wave_path therefore treats
every branch/jump edge as traversable and only an indirect exit as unsafe;
the reduction gate and a first-lane read on the same path use it.

Offline check with the containers the last run spilled (0a5d4f90,
a53a7977, 1369868128, ce2378e5, be14e72d): all five now translate
(182796, 493668, 46136, 31684, 455288 byte DXIL). Test: a lane branch is
wave_path-uniform but not uniform_control-uniform. Host tests pass.
